{
  "id": "decibel_a__b_and_c",
  "title": "Decibel A, B and C",
  "description": "Calculator for Decibel A, B and C sound pressure level filters. The human ear is more sensitive to sound in the 1 to 4 kHz frequency range. This tool helps compensate for human hearing using A, B, and C weighted decibel filters commonly used in sound measurement.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Decibel A, B and C Sound Filters\n\nThe human ear is more sensitive to sound in the _1 to 4 kHz_ frequency range than to sound at very low or very high frequencies. Sound meters use filters to adapt measured sound response to human hearing:\n\n- **dB(A)**: Most widely used, corresponds to 40 dB equal-loudness curve\n- **dB(B)**: Between A and C, rarely used\n- **dB(C)**: Practically linear, suitable for high sound pressure levels\n\nThis calculator helps you work with these decibel-weighted measurements."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "measured_level",
          "label": "Measured Sound Pressure Level",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "dB",
          "defaultValue": 50
        },
        {
          "id": "frequency",
          "label": "Frequency",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "31.25 Hz",
              "value": 31.25
            },
            {
              "label": "62.5 Hz",
              "value": 62.5
            },
            {
              "label": "125 Hz",
              "value": 125
            },
            {
              "label": "250 Hz",
              "value": 250
            },
            {
              "label": "500 Hz",
              "value": 500
            },
            {
              "label": "1000 Hz",
              "value": 1000
            },
            {
              "label": "2000 Hz",
              "value": 2000
            },
            {
              "label": "4000 Hz",
              "value": 4000
            },
            {
              "label": "8000 Hz",
              "value": 8000
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "filter_type",
          "label": "Decibel Filter Type",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "dB(A)",
              "value": "A"
            },
            {
              "label": "dB(B)",
              "value": "B"
            },
            {
              "label": "dB(C)",
              "value": "C"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "A"
        },
        {
          "id": "context_adjustment",
          "label": "Context Adjustment",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "dB",
          "defaultValue": 0
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "weighted_level",
          "label": "Weighted Sound Pressure Level",
          "formula": "inputs.measured_level + inputs.context_adjustment",
          "unit": "dB",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Frequency (Hz)",
        "dB(A) Filter (dB)",
        "dB(B) Filter (dB)",
        "dB(C) Filter (dB)"
      ],
